# Ran and Shaw (legendary 4/4 Dragon, flying, firebending 2): "When Ran and Shaw enter, if you cast them and there are three or
# more Dragon and/or Lesson cards in your graveyard, create a token that's a copy of Ran and Shaw, except it's not legendary."
# On turn 3 Bot1 kills Bot2's three Ornithopters with three Firebending Lessons (so three Lesson cards are in its graveyard),
# and on turn 7 casts Ran and Shaw: the token copy enters too and, being not legendary, the legend rule leaves both (CR 704.5j).
# The token was not cast, so its own enters trigger does nothing, and only the one copy is made.

